RUN_COMPLETE: venmo-for-lonely-retirees

- **Rolled:** Venmo for lonely retirees, with no rerolls. The product is **Tuppence**, a payments app where you "send $1.50 and four paragraphs to anyone who will accept it."
- **Design:** Very large type styled as a "large print edition", with a working A / A+ / A++ text-size control that rescales the whole page. Colours are ultramarine and highlighter yellow on a pale bank-cheque blue; fonts are Inter Tight for headings and Atkinson Hyperlegible for body text. It doesn't repeat the style, palette or fonts of any of the last 7 entries.
- **Images:** I made 3 testimonial headshots and all passed the visual check on the first try. The demo feed reuses them as avatars. I skipped the hero image because the design is all type.
- **Demo:** A payment feed you can filter with tabs and search. It has hearts, expandable memos, and live countdowns for payments waiting on a callback. The Pay/Request form won't send until the memo reaches 280 characters, and a sent payment appears at the top of the feed.
- **Validation:** The first run failed. The demo built its `<img>` tags in JavaScript, and the validator read that code as a missing image file. I fixed it and the rerun passed.
- **Records:** I appended the entry to `state/history.json` and added the run summary to `state/runs/2026-09-28.log`. I added to the end of the log rather than overwriting it, because the wrapper also writes there.
- **Gallery:** I rebuilt it with 107 entries. Apart from the new slide and the count, the only change is that two entries dated June 12 swapped places.
- **No git commands run**, as instructed.

